==English==

===Etymology===
Past participle of {{m|en|embarrass}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪmˈbæɹ.əst/|a=UK,US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɪmˈbɛɹ.əst/|a=US,Mary-marry-merry}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Having a feeling of [[shameful]] discomfort.
#: {{ant|en|honored|proud}}
#: {{cot|en|ashamed|shy}}
#: {{ux|en|After returning from the pool, Aleshia felt significantly better, though she was still slightly '''embarrassed'''.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} Impeded; obstructed; in an [[awkward]] situation.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1897|author=Henry James|title=What Maisie Knew|passage={{...}} they could let their eyes hover tenderly on the far-off white cliffs that so often had signalled to the '''embarrassed''' English a promise of safety.}}

